{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Upon Mount Sinai.</b> The Torah was not given in the land of Israel, so that the nations would not have an opening of the mouth to say: because it was not given in our land, we did not accept it upon ourselves. Another interpretation: if the Torah had been given in the land of Israel, there would have been jealousy among the tribes — this one saying, it was given in my portion, and that one saying, it was given in my portion. And the סין of Scripture is Sinai; after the Ten Commandments were given upon it, its name was called Sinai."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:50.920880034Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}